# C2-S1 fix round 1: gate P2 fixed, every lane green

The gate's P2 is fixed: a `yield` in a nested definition's header now makes the enclosing function a generator. JVM, Node and Dart all pass, and kondo and cljstyle are clean. Nothing is staged or committed.

## The fix (`src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc`)
- **`definition-body`** returns the part of a `def`, `class` or `lambda` that runs in its own scope (the `block`, or a lambda's last expression).
- **`yields?`** looks for a `yield` that belongs to the current scope:
  - When it meets a nested definition, it scans the definition's header (parameter defaults and annotations, class bases) but not its body.
  - Yields inside nested bodies still don't count, as before.
- **`generator-body?`** is now `(yields? ctx (definition-body ctx scope-node))`.
- The lowering itself needed no change: defaults and class bases were already lowered in the enclosing context, so their `yield` uses the enclosing function's generator binder.

## Regression tests
- **`lower_test.clj`, new `generator-classification-test`.** It checks which functions are lowered as generators:

  | Case | Lowered as generator |
  |---|---|
  | Function default holds the enclosing function's only yield | `g` |
  | Lambda default holds the only yield | `g` |
  | Class base holds the only yield | `g` |
  | Yield in a default and in the nested body | `g` and `h` |
  | Enclosing body also yields, plus a yield in a default | `g` |
  | Yield only in a nested function body | `h` |
  | Yield only in a lambda body | `<lambda>` |

  The negative control, a yield only in a nested class body, still gives `'yield' outside function`.
- **`e2e_c2_test.clj`, new `yield-in-nested-default-test`.** `def h(x=(yield 1))` inside `g`: `next` gives `1`, and `send('d')` becomes the default, printing `1 d` on all four VMs.

