## Deviations from your instructions
- **I ran the JVM lane as chunks, not as one `bb test:clj` command.** The full lane takes over 35 minutes, and the harness caps a foreground command at 10 minutes, then moves it to the background. So I ran the lane's two dependency builds (`bb gen:python-antlr`, `bb build:yin-repl-node`) and then `clojure -M:test` over nine namespace regexes, each in the foreground. Together they cover every JVM test namespace.
- **The Dart lane ran in the background.** I started it in the foreground; it passed the 10-minute cap and the harness moved it to the background. It is one compile plus `dart test`, so it can't be split. I left it running and waited in this turn with a foreground loop until it exited.
- **One chunk was stopped and re-run.** My first `yin.(?!vm)` chunk also hit the cap and was moved to the background. I stopped it before it finished and re-ran that range as the four smaller chunks listed above.

